o see us both you know  singing and dance on our way across  raider city stage is something pretty  pretty cool pretty iconic and i think in  general like this is my first experience  coming out to new york and being a part  of the broadway community and that's  exactly what it is the the community is  so generous and kind and welcoming but  i'll say also after the last couple  years like broadway coming back in the  75th anniversary i mean this is truly an  honor to be able to be asked to to host  this first act at the tony awards so  it's pretty cool we have a lot of  excitement in the house and we're also  returning radio city music yes that's  right  and set the stage and speaking of which  you you wrote the music and the lyrics  for your opening number yeah  what was that process like uh well i  mean i've i've i started my my way in  the entertainment uh  bowling alley as where i don't know if  it's called that uh  but you just coined it yeah sure i don't  know i i sort of cut my teeth as a  songwriter and as a composer and so i've  as a theater nerd i've always wanted to  write a song for the tonys and so when  they asked me to post this i was like  all right there's a quid pro quo here uh  i if i'll do it if you let me write the  opening number and so jules and i are  doing the song called set the stage and  that'll be opening the whole the whole  shebang very cool  theater people are the most fun people  you mentioned the community if i could  do high school again forget sports i  would be a theater nerd for for no you  wouldn't i was somebody who's a theater  and who got like i won't say beat up but  who got harassed a lot by these by the  jocks  i don't know bro you wouldn't want to  trade places with me i would definitely  the parties were much better in  retrospect also the long-term effects  we'll just put it that way  segment we can yeah  you are who you hang out with uh i want  to ask about your pre-show rituals i'm  fascinated by them you put on a great  song jules just dance away how did that  start yeah you know i mean  like anything i love to have a ritual  before i go on stage just so it like  puts me in that zone connects me to that  performance for every night and i love  connection and so to be able to share  this the moment with all of our  incredible cast members and you know  it's all about you know figuring out  what they want so i'll send a note to  them being like what's the song for  today and um yeah it's just fun it just  kind of became our thing and um they  they always know at 7 30 i'm gonna be  blasting music throughout the the  theater so  just coming in hot with something it's a  lot cleaner than ours  how you seeing it you're just looking at  it now you're like wait a second i gotta  i gotta  yeah what do you do before a show uh i  mean it does it definitely doesn't look  as cool as that although sam rockwell is  a terrific dancer and he will he'll  definitely cut a rug we'll blast some  funk music but backstage you know uh  lawrence fishburne is a very  nimble athletic man so i i try and copy  him when he does all this kind of tai  chi kind of stuff every now and then  he'll he'll shoot me a morpheus he'll do  one of those oh my gosh and i squeal  inside it's very strange well you know  vanessa williams is a part of our show  too and like  again legend iconic but she started  dancing and ballroom dancing and that  was the first person that i ever saw in  ballroom dancing in a movie and so like  we we actually you know backstage we're  dancing leah delaria julie white rachel  dratch i mean it's like the craziest  cast and so just getting together and  you know cutting a rug it's the best  yeah no vanessa and dance with me i  thought yeah that was the movie yeah it  was a great movie but  your broadway debut is potus quickly why  did you choose it you know i think it's  always been a dream of mine to  be on broadway and i didn't want to just  do it as like a bucket list like i mean  i'm out